   - Negotiate vendor contracts & payment terms (deferments, discounts for prepay) — one-time cash relief + monthly savings.
   - Tighten procurement approvals and freeze new capital purchases.

   Expected impact: 5–15% reduction in net burn quickly.

2. Medium-term / structural (3–9 months)
   - Role prioritization and selective headcount reductions or attrition-based reshaping (target lower-performing roles or hires not yet started) — often largest single savings (can be 20–50% of payroll portion).
   - Office footprint optimization (sublease space / shift to hybrid) — meaningful recurring savings if physical space is large.
   - Consolidate SaaS and platform costs, optimize cloud spend — can cut 10–30% of those budgets with optimization.
   - Repricing, packaging changes, or upsell programs to increase ARPU.

   Expected impact: 15–40% reduction depending on aggressiveness.

3. Revenue / cash-acceleration levers (0–6 months)
   - Short-term promotions, upsell & retention campaigns to increase near-term revenue.
   - Tighten collections (AR days), accelerate invoicing, require deposits for large projects.
   - Pursue smaller commercial deals or strategic pilots which convert quickly.

   Expected impact: improves cash inflow and reduces net burn; even 10–25% revenue uplift materially reduces net burn.

4. Financing options (non-cost but runway-extending)
   - Venture debt or a short-term bridge loan — preserves equity, adds runway quickly; watch covenants and interest.
