- Hiring freeze on open roles and pause all non-essential contractor renewals — immediate monthly savings variable but typically 5–15% of payroll spend.
- Pause or cut discretionary spend: travel, events, conferences, non-critical marketing campaigns.
- SaaS/tool audit: cancel unused/duplicative subscriptions and renegotiate vendor terms (annual prepay discounts, lower tiers).
- Collections and AP timing: accelerate collections (incentives for early payment), tighten payment terms; negotiate longer-pay terms with vendors.

Medium term / 30–90 days (moderate action & approvals)
- Vendor renegotiations and volume discounts for recurring services.
- Office and real-estate: switch to flexible space, negotiate lease concessions, sublet unused space.
- Marketing optimization: shift spend to highest-ROI channels, pause low-return programs.
- Comp & bonus deferrals: temporary pause of non-essential bonuses, defer raises where feasible.

Higher impact / 60–120 days (may include headcount changes)
- Targeted headcount realignment: voluntary departure packages, selective layoffs focused on non-revenue or low-productivity roles. Use role-by-role ROI analysis (cost vs. revenue or strategic value).
- Outsource / convert full-time roles to contractors where appropriate.
- Defer major product initiatives or capital expenditures that aren’t mission-critical.

Typical savings estimates (these are very dependent on your cost structure — use as a rule-of-thumb):
- Hiring freeze + contractor pause: 5–10% immediate reduction in monthly burn.
