B — Concrete runway-extension & cost-reduction options (with math/examples)

1) Immediate (0–3 months) — low friction / fastest cash impact
- Hiring freeze + pause contractor spend
  - Example: freeze hiring for 6 months saving $40K/month in net payroll + contractors → burn drops to 22K/month (62–40 = 22K) → runway = 1.2M / 22K ≈ 54.5 months.
- Reduce discretionary spend (marketing events, travel, recruiting, conferences)
  - Example: cut $10K/month → burn = 52K → runway ≈ 23.1 months (+3.1 months).
- SaaS/cloud cost audit and cuts
  - Target 10–20% reduction in tooling/cloud. If you cut $6K–$12K/month → runway improves by ~0.1–0.2 months per $6K saved, but still meaningful over time.
- Tighten collections & accelerate receivables
  - Offer 1–2% discount for 30-day prepayments for large customers; converting one $200K receivable to prepayment adds immediate cash.
- Freeze discretionary hiring bonuses and travel allowances (quick $ savings).

2) Near-term (3–6 months) — moderate changes with bigger savings
- Vendor renegotiation (licenses, agency, office lease)
  - Example: renegotiate office/lease or terminate subleases to save $15K/month → burn = 47K → runway ≈ 25.5 months.
- Convert full-time roles to fixed-term or part-time, or move some work to freelancers where cost-effective
  - Replacing $30K/month of payroll with $15K/month contractors saves $15K/month → runway ≈ 28.6 months.
- Reduce marketing spend mix to high-ROI channels only; pause brand initiatives.
- Reprice or bundle products for short-term uplift (see revenue section).

3) Medium-term (6–12 months) — structural changes
- Role consolidation and targeted headcount reductions (if needed)
  - Example: cutting $100K/year per eliminated role → ~ $8.3K/month. Removing 6 roles (~$600K/yr) saves $50K/month → burn = 12K → runway = 100 months (but this is an extreme example — use carefully).
- Benefits/cost restructuring (move to performance-heavy comp, defer bonuses into equity)
- Office footprint optimization (hybrid or remote shift to eliminate rent)
- Strategic partnerships and channel sales to accelerate large deals

4) Fundraising & financing (parallel/short timeline options)
- Small bridge / VC friends-and-family / existing investors
  - To buy N additional months: Additional Cash Needed ≈ N × 62K.
  - Example: to gain +12 months → ~ $744K; to gain +6 months → ~ $372K.
- Venture debt / line of credit
  - Works if you have revenue traction and predictable receipts; cheaper and faster but requires covenants.
- Revenue-based financing / invoice factoring
  - Unlocks receivables; dilution-free but higher effective cost.
- Non-dilutive grants, R&D tax credits, reimbursements
  - One-time boosts to cash — good to pursue in parallel.
- Strategic prepayments / customer financing
  - Negotiate multi-quarter prepayments in exchange for discounts or added services.

