"Stellar Labs enters the quarter with $1.2M in cash and a current net cash burn of roughly $62K/month, giving us approximately 20 months of runway at current spending. Over the next 90 days we will implement a prioritized plan to extend runway and accelerate revenue: (1) immediate hiring freeze and $X/month discretionary cuts to capture quick savings, (2) renegotiate vendor contracts and reduce low-ROI marketing to drive a 20–30% reduction in net burn, and (3) pursue a modest bridge financing of ~$750K–$1.5M while accelerating enterprise sales and prepayment offers. These actions together are projected to extend our runway to 3+ years while preserving product momentum and our core GTM investment. We expect to report back with detailed scenario modeling and headcount-tailored plans within two weeks."

