"Stellar Labs enters this quarter with $1.2M cash and ~20 months of runway based on our current net burn of $62K/month. Our analysis shows we can extend runway to ~36 months through a modest mix of actions: a ~10% reduction in operating expenses (largely discretionary and vendor spend) OR ~13% revenue uplift, or a balanced combination (e.g., 5–7% cost cuts + 5–10% revenue growth). We recommend immediate actions (hiring freeze, vendor renegotiations, AR acceleration) to buy time, while pursuing targeted revenue initiatives and preparing a bridge fundraise of ~$1.0–1.2M as a contingency. Proposed KPIs and triggers will ensure we act ahead of cash constraints."

Expanded (2–3 paragraphs for more detail)
"Current position: Cash $1.2M, net burn $62K/month → ~20 months runway. Implied monthly expense base is ~$285K and monthly revenue ~$223K. Given that revenue already covers the majority of our cost base, only modest operational improvements or revenue gains materially extend runway.

Recommended plan: (1) Immediate actions (0–90 days) — implement a hiring freeze, renegotiate vendor contracts, reduce discretionary spend, and accelerate receivables (offers for annual prepayments). (2) Near-term revenue focus — prioritize enterprise deals, upsell existing customers, and test targeted price increases. (3) Financing contingency — prepare a bridge round of ~$1.0–1.2M or evaluate venture-debt/revenue-based finance to avoid forced cuts. With a 5–7% expense reduction plus 5–10% revenue growth we project runway extending well beyond 36 months, with manageable organizational impact. We will track weekly cash, net burn, AR days, and pipeline conversion; if any key trigger is breached we will escalate to the board."

7) Next steps I can do for you
