- 10% cost cut + 10% revenue growth:
  - Expenses = 256,800; revenue = 245,667
  - Net burn = 11,133 / month
  - Runway = 1,200,000 / 11,133 = 107.8 months

Key insight: Because monthly revenue (~$223k) is large relative to the current $62k net burn, modest percentage changes in expenses or revenue produce outsized effects on runway. Small operational wins or a modest acceleration of revenue can move you to break-even or cash-positive quickly.

3) Practical cost-reduction levers (prioritized, with impact/risks)
- Near-term, low-friction (quick wins)
  - Hiring freeze + pause non-critical contractors (immediate monthly savings)
  - Freeze discretionary spend (travel, conferences, non-product marketing)
  - Renegotiate vendor contracts / SaaS licenses, delay renewals
  - Tighten procurement approvals
  - Improve collections & tighten payment terms (accelerates cash inflows)
