- Execute quick wins (hiring freeze, vendor renegotiation, collections push) to buy headroom while pursuing revenue acceleration.
- Parallel-track financing conversations (venture debt + convertible bridge) so you’re ready if growth does not accelerate as planned.
- Weekly cash and KPI reporting to Exec + Board: cash balance, runway, net burn, MRR/ARR, gross margin, DSO, top-10 customers concentration.

7) Finance narrative (short, board-friendly draft)
Executive summary (2–3 sentences):
- “Stellar Labs enters this period with $1.2M in cash and a reported ~20 months of runway on a net burn of $62K/month. Our revenue run-rate is strong (last quarter = $670K), which gives high leverage: modest cost optimization or revenue acceleration can push us to cash neutrality or growth quickly. We recommend a two-track plan: immediate operational savings to secure runway and an aggressive commercial push to convert revenue momentum into cash inflows; concurrently prepare financing backup (venture debt / bridge) if needed.”

