- Immediate (0–30 days): hiring freeze, renegotiate top vendor contracts, accelerate collections. Rationale: low-friction moves that materially reduce net burn.
- Near-term (30–90 days): prioritize enterprise upsells, offer annual prepayment discounts, focus on top 20% of customers. Rationale: revenue growth quickly reduces net burn and increases leverage with lenders/investors.
- Finance contingency: open venture debt discussions and one convertible note term sheet. Rationale: shorten time-to-close if market windows tighten.

KPIs to track for the board:
- Cash balance, runway (months), net burn, monthly revenue (and growth %), DSO, customer concentration, CAC payback.

