Estimated impact (example): a mix of hiring freeze + contractors cut + marketing freeze + SaaS cleanup often yields 10–20% monthly burn reduction quickly.

B. Medium term (30–90 days; moderate impact)
- Restructure vendor contracts / renegotiate pricing and payment terms (defer cash outflows) — 2–10% savings, improved near-term cash.
- Reassess office footprint (move to smaller space or renegotiate lease) — 5–25% depending on situation.
- Convert discretionary bonuses into equity or defer payouts — one-time cash retention.
- Optimize product roadmap to reduce burn tied to low-priority projects.

C. Deeper / strategic (60–120+ days; larger impact but higher cost)
- Headcount reductions or targeted layoffs (if necessary) — large save but high one-time costs (severance). Could produce 20–50% of savings if headcount is the largest cost.
