- Vendor & subscription audit: cancel redundant SaaS, consolidate, negotiate discounts — savings often 5–20% of those line items.
- Capital expense deferrals: delay noncritical purchases, software licenses, and upgrades.
Medium-term (30–90 days)
- Renegotiate vendor contracts and payment terms (extend payables to preserve cash).
- Re-scope or pause lower-priority product projects; concentrate on revenue-driving features.
- Convert contractors to part-time or fixed deliverable contracts.
- Office/site consolidation or negotiate rent deferral.
Lower-immediate-impact / structural (60–120+ days)
- Role consolidation or selective layoffs (last resort; high impact but high morale cost).
- Salary adjustments/temporary salary reductions (with clear sunset and leadership participation).
- Move to variable comp or commission for some sales roles to reduce fixed costs.
