“Stellar Labs is starting QX with $1.2M in cash and an estimated 20 months of runway based on a current net burn of ~$62K/month. Revenue last quarter was $670K and covers a substantial portion of operating expenses, so modest revenue growth or targeted expense reductions can materially increase runway. We propose a two-track plan: (1) immediate actions to preserve cash and reduce net burn by 10–20% (hiring freeze, vendor renegotiation, SaaS consolidation, pause low-ROI marketing) and (2) revenue acceleration initiatives (enterprise upsells, annual prepayments, shorten sales cycle). If implemented, the combined program should extend runway to 24–30+ months while we evaluate non-dilutive financing or a modest bridge as contingency. We are requesting approval to implement immediate cuts and to prepare investor materials should we need to pursue a bridge within 90 days.”

Three-slide suggested content
- Slide 1: Current position & key metrics: cash, net burn, runway, revenue last quarter, implied runway chart + sensitivity (burn cuts & revenue uplift table).
- Slide 2: Proposed actions (Immediate / Short-term / Medium-term), expected % burn reduction by category, and timeline to impact.
- Slide 3: Financing options & recommended next steps (non-dilutive first, prepare bridge docs, target runway goal e.g., 24–36 months).

