“Our current position is solid: $1.2M in cash with approximately 20 months of runway at our current net burn of $62K/month. That gives us breathing room to execute, but we recommend a two-pronged plan to materially strengthen the balance sheet and accelerate our path to cash-neutral operations: (1) implement targeted, time‑boxed operating cost reductions and a hiring freeze to reduce non-essential spend, and (2) prioritize revenue initiatives (annual prepayments, enterprise conversions, and collections improvements) that increase high-margin cash receipts. Under a conservative combined scenario (10% cost reduction + focused sales acceleration), we project we convert to net-positive cash within quarters and extend runway significantly — while minimizing long-term damage to growth and product delivery. We are also preparing contingency financing options (bridge financing or customer prepayments) if market conditions or execution risks require additional liquidity. Recommended next step: approve the immediate 30-day cost and collection actions so finance can produce a detailed 90-day cash plan and a board-ready materials package.”

