B. Scenario math (fast reference)
I’ll show the effect of expense cuts and raises on runway. Formula: runway (months) = cash / monthly burn.

Baseline (your numbers)
- Monthly burn = $62,000 → runway ≈ 19.35 months (≈20 months).

Expense reduction scenarios (no additional cash raised)
- 20% cut: new burn = 62,000 * 0.80 = $49,600 → runway = 1,200,000 / 49,600 ≈ 24.2 months (+ ~4.8 months).
- 30% cut: new burn = $43,400 → runway ≈ 27.7 months (+ ~8.4 months).
- 40% cut: new burn = $37,200 → runway ≈ 32.3 months (+ ~13 months).

Raise scenarios (no cuts)
