Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Good — I can help. Below I’ll (1) reconcile the numbers, (2) show runway-extension targets and what reductions or financing are required, (3) list concrete cost-reduction and revenue-acceleration levers with rough impact estimates and risks, (4) give a prioritized 30/90/180-day action plan, and (5) provide a short finance narrative you can use in internal materials. Tell me if you want this turned into a one-page memo or slides and I’ll draft them.

1) Reconcile current position
- Cash: $1.2M
- Stated burn: $62K/month (I’ll assume this is net cash burn after operating revenue and receipts; if it’s non‑net, tell me)
- Stated runway: ~20 months. Calculation: 1,200,000 / 62,000 = 19.35 months (≈19–20 months). So your 20-month statement is consistent (rounded).

Additional helpful datapoints to confirm: is the $62K the net monthly cash burn (cash outflows minus cash inflows)? Are there any committed near-term large cash items (leases, capex, bonuses)? If not, I’ll proceed assuming net burn.

2) Runway extension math (targets and required monthly burn)
- Current runway ≈ 19.4 months at $62K/mo.
- Target runway → Required net burn (given $1.2M cash):
  - 24 months: burn = 1,200,000 / 24 = $50K/mo → required reduction = $12K/mo (≈19% cut)
  - 30 months: burn = 1,200,000 / 30 = $40K/mo → required reduction = $22K/mo (≈35% cut)
  - 36 months: burn = 1,200,000 / 36 = $33.3K/mo → reduction = $28.7K/mo (≈46% cut)

