Immediate (0–30 days — quick wins, low permanent impact)
- Hiring freeze & contractor audit: stop all nonessential hiring. Renegotiate contractor scope or rates. Impact: often 5–15% of OPEX within 30 days.
- Suspend discretionary spend: events, travel, conferences, noncritical software trials. Impact: 1–5% of OPEX immediately.
- Vendor & lease renegotiation: ask for payment terms, discounts, deferred payments. Impact: depends on contracts — can free working capital.

Near-term (30–90 days — structural savings)
- SaaS / tools consolidation: eliminate unused seats/licenses and negotiate enterprise pricing. Impact: 1–6% of OPEX.
- Reduce marketing spend but focus on high-ROI channels: move budgets to performance marketing that converts quickly; pause brand campaigns. Impact: 5–15% of marketing spend with minimal revenue impact if targeted.
- Headcount / role rebalancing: consider targeted reductions (reduce management layers, contractors first). Impact: large (10–40% of payroll depending on scope) but high employee impact.

Medium-term (90+ days — strategic but slower)
- Rethink office footprint: shift to hybrid, sublet space, renegotiate lease. Impact: meaningful for large real estate lines.
- Outsource/nearshore non-core functions: customer support, back office. Impact: reduces FTE costs and convert fixed to variable.
- Reprioritize product R&D: delay non-critical features; focus on revenue-driving and retention work. Impact: reduces near-term spend while protecting growth bets.

Tactical cash-preservation moves
- Offer customers discounts for annual prepayment / extend contracts for upfront cash.
- Improve collections (shorten payment terms, early-pay incentives).
- Defer capital expenditures and nonessential vendor payments with negotiated plans.
- Capitalize certain R&D costs if accounting policy permits (check accounting/GAAP).

3) Runway-extension and financing options (non‑mutually exclusive)
Non-dilutive / low-dilution options
- Accelerate receivables / invoice factoring or get bridge from customers in exchange for discounts.
- Government grants / R&D tax credits, if eligible.
- Venture debt or revenue-based financing: can extend runway without immediate dilution; usually requires ~12–18 months runway and some traction (your revenue is attractive).
- Strategic partnerships / customer-funded pilots: partners pay to co-develop or accelerate deployment.

Equity / dilution options
- Small bridge round (friends & family / existing investors / insiders) to cover shortfall or to create target runway (e.g., $300K to hit 24 months).
- Full equity round: larger, more runway but more process/time and dilution — start process 6–9 months before you need to close.

Fundraising timing recommendation
