- Option B (reduce burn): allowed burn = 1.2M / 30 = $40,000/month → required reduction = 22k/month (≈35% reduction)
- Option C (mix): e.g., raise $300k + reduce burn 12%: new cash 1.5M, new burn 54.6k → runway = 1.5M / 54.6k ≈ 27.5 months

Quick sensitivity table (examples)
- 20 months: no change (current)
- 24 months: raise $288k OR cut ~19% ($12k/mo)
- 30 months: raise $660k OR cut ~35% ($22k/mo) OR mix smaller raise + smaller cuts

C. Concrete runway-extension and cost-reduction levers (prioritised)
Priority 1 — Fast, low-friction actions (0–30 days)
- Hiring freeze (pause new hires & open reqs). Impact: immediate monthly savings depending on roles.
- Freeze raises / bonuses and non-essential discretionary spend (events, travel).
- SaaS and vendor audit: cancel unused subscriptions, negotiate 10–30% discounts or extended payment terms. Quick savings target: $3k–$10k+/mo.
- Cloud / infrastructure optimization: rightsizing instances, reserved instances, auto-scaling policies. Typical savings 10–30% of cloud spend.
- Collections / AR acceleration: tighten payment terms, incentivize early payment, factor receivables. Improves cash balance immediately.

Priority 2 — Medium-term operational changes (30–90 days)
- Vendor renegotiation for milestone-based payments, longer terms, or lower rates.
- Convert contractors to temporary part-time or finish-off contractors to save 10–40% of contractor costs.
- Marketing & GTM re-focus: shift spend to highest-converting channels; pause low-ROI campaigns.
- Pause or defer noncritical capital projects or product initiatives.
- Renegotiate leases or office footprint (remote/hybrid) — reduce real estate costs.

Priority 3 — Structural changes (60–120 days)
- Headcount optimization (targeted reductions where productivity < cost or overlapping roles). Model severance and one-time costs; aim for net monthly savings thereafter.
- Role consolidation and temporary furloughs if culturally feasible.
- Outsourcing / nearshoring back-office functions (finance, HR) for lower cost.

Priority 4 — Financing alternatives (30–90 days)
- Venture debt or revenue-based financing: faster than equity, less dilution; typical raise size: $300k–$2M depending on covenants. Factor monthly interest/service costs into the burn model.
- Bridge round / SAFE: raise $288k–$660k as needed to hit targets (dilution depends on valuation).
- Non-dilutive funding: R&D tax credits, grant programs, government loans.
- Line of credit or factoring AR to smooth cash flow.

