Medium term (3–9 months)
- Role consolidation and org redesign (natural attrition + selective layoffs if necessary): largest single source of savings but highest cultural impact. Quantify by FTE cost.
- Shift compensation mix (defer bonuses, increase equity component).
- Optimize GTM: focus on higher-margin segments, upsells, packaging changes.
- Consider office footprint reduction (remote-first): saves 10–30% of office costs.

Estimated quick-impact savings example (illustrative)
- Hiring freeze / contractor pause: $30k–$60k/month
- Marketing optimization: $10k–$40k/month
- Vendor renegotiation & SaaS trimming: $5k–$20k/month
- AR & payment terms improvement (one-time cash): $100k+ depending on receivables
Combine 1–3 of the above and you can plausibly target a 10%+ reduction quickly (which per the math materially extends runway).

Recommended two-track approach (practical & defensible)
1) Immediate “buy time” actions (within 30 days):
   - Implement hiring freeze, pause nonessential contractor work, cut discretionary spend, and push for faster collections and vendor payment renegotiation.
   - Target: reduce net burn 20–40% or secure ~3–6 months of additional cushion via cash conservation + AR conversion.
