- Tradeoffs: Aggressive cost cuts (headcount) materially extend runway but slow growth. A modest raise reduces the need for painful cuts, at the cost of dilution. We recommend a balanced approach — conserve cash with non-headcount measures first, start a targeted raise, and only pursue deeper structural cuts if financing options are limited.
- Ask of leadership/board: Approve immediate hiring freeze and vendor payment negotiation; authorize finance to pursue a bridge of $400k (or alternatives) and return in 6 weeks with P&L scenario updates.

