- "Request: leadership approval to execute the immediate measures and authority to open negotiations for financing if savings fall short of target. We will report weekly on cash, 13-week forecast, and milestone progress."

One-paragraph supporting detail (for slide)
- Current cash is $1.2M with runway ~19–20 months. Short-term actions focus on low-friction savings and cash collection to extend runway quickly; medium-term actions address structural cost optimization and revenue acceleration. If we achieve a 20–25% burn reduction, we extend runway by roughly 5–8 months, putting the company in a position to either close a growth financing on stronger terms or execute strategic investments into growth channels.

Metrics & governance to include in materials
- Weekly cash balance, 13-week cash forecast, monthly burn (pre/post initiatives), revenue velocity (bookings, ARR), DSO, top 10 cost line items and progress on reductions, hiring pipeline status, and fundraising milestones (if applicable).

E. Recommended next steps (what I can help prepare)
