- 25% burn cut → burn $46,500 → runway ≈ 25.8 months (+6.4 months)
- 40% burn cut → burn $37,200 → runway ≈ 32.3 months (+12.9 months)
- 50% burn cut → burn $31,000 → runway ≈ 38.7 months (+19.3 months)

Fundraise scenarios (no cost change):
- Raise $500K → cash $1.7M → runway = 1,700,000 / 62,000 ≈ 27.4 months
- Raise $1M → cash $2.2M → runway ≈ 35.5 months

Combined examples:
- Raise $500K + 25% cost cut → cash 1.7M, burn 46.5K → runway ≈ 36.6 months
- Add $30K/month net new cash from revenue initiatives (i.e., reduce net burn by $30K): burn becomes 32K → runway = 1.2M / 32K = 37.5 months

Use these to set target asks: e.g., to reach 24 months runway you could either: raise ~$200K (1.4M/62K ≈ 22.6 months; more precise: target 24 months requires cash = 24*62K = $1.488M → raise ≈ $288K) — or cut burn ~20% (burn → $49.6K → runway 24.2 months).

