- Near-term (30–90d): vendor renegotiations, convert contractors to project basis, prioritize high-ROI marketing/sales.
- Medium-term (90–180d): headcount optimization if needed, evaluate real estate, consider restructuring large contracts.
- Financing: begin a small bridge or pre-emptive raise now (e.g., $1M target) while preparing for an opportunistic larger round if growth accelerates.

4) Scenarios with outcomes (be explicit)
- Base: no change → ~19–20 months.
- Modest cuts (20% burn reduction) → ~24 months runway — buys time to reach next growth inflection with minimal dilution.
- Raise $1M now → extends runway to ~35 months, allowing growth investments and optionality.
- Combined 20% cut + $1M raise → runway ~44 months; very conservative.

5) Ask / decisions for board or leadership
- Approve immediate cost-savings package (list of items).
- Set target runway (suggest 24 months) and fundraising posture (soft market outreach now).
- Agree to weekly cash reporting cadence and a decision date for any headcount choices (e.g., 60 days).

6) Risks & mitigation
- Risk: revenue variability — mitigate by focusing on recurring revenue and shortening sales cycles.
- Risk: talent loss after cuts — mitigate by clear communication, short-term retention incentives for critical roles.

G. Operational checklist & KPIs to present
- Weekly cash balance and runway (best-case, base-case, worst-case).
