- To reach 36 months at current burn: need 36*62k = $2,232,000 → shortfall = $1,032,000

3) Practical cost-reduction and runway-extension levers (prioritized)
I. Quick / low-friction (0–30 days)
- Hiring freeze for open roles — immediate savings = monthly hire cost avoided. Impact: ~low friction, high certainty.
- Pause non-essential marketing campaigns and events — savings $5k–$30k/mo (depending on spend).
- SaaS/vendor audit & renegotiate/cancel underused subscriptions — savings $2k–$15k/mo.
- Delay discretionary capital spend and software purchases — immediate cash flow relief.

II. Medium-term (30–90 days)
- Renegotiate large vendor contracts (payment terms, deferred payments) — can free 1–3 months cash.
- Reduce contractor/agency hours; convert to part-time or project-based — savings $5k–$30k/mo.
- Temporary reductions in variable comp / hiring bonuses or defer bonuses — savings vary.
- Sublease or reduce office footprint where possible — savings $3k–$20k/mo.

III. Significant / strategic (90+ days)
- Headcount optimization (performance-based layoffs / voluntary separation packages) — largest single lever; each FTE avoided saves the monthly fully-loaded cost (estimate your avg fully loaded cost per FTE and multiply). Example: if fully loaded avg = $12k/month, removing 5 FTE = ~$60k/mo.
- Programme reprioritization in R&D: pause non-core features or postpone hires — savings $10k–$100k+/mo depending on scale.
- Outsource at lower cost or offshore certain functions — savings depend on function and quality tradeoff.

